      "widgets_values": [
        "Create a 10-second, 16:9 cinematic technology short called “Axon Signal.” No\nexisting characters, brands, logos, or copyrighted designs.\n\nVisual anchor: an original gender-neutral field engineer in a matte graphite\nutility suit with one thin amber signal line across the shoulder. Their face,\nclothing, proportions, and amber accent remain consistent.\n\n[0–3s] Extreme close-up of a small black signal prism waking in the engineer's\ngloved hand. A single amber pulse travels through etched channels. Slow camera\npullback reveals a quiet brutalist observatory at blue hour.\n\n[3–7s] The engineer walks toward a circular antenna. The camera tracks at waist\nheight. The amber pulse leaves the prism, travels along the floor, and climbs\nthe antenna as one physically coherent line. Wind moves the coat fabric.\n\n[7–10s] Wide shot: the antenna emits one restrained amber ring across a dark\ncloud layer. The engineer remains clearly visible in the foreground. End on a\nstable composition, not a cut to black.\n\nAudio: native stereo. Low electrical hum, precise relay clicks, wind across\nconcrete, one deep analog pulse at 7 seconds, then a clean unresolved tone. No\ndialogue and no recognizable music. No text, captions, logos, watermarks,\nextra limbs, random camera spins, neon cyberpunk city, or explosive particles.",
        1344,
        768,
        73
      ]
    }
